{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Scale-invariance gate for the SUBSURFACE path (spec 10.2 phase 3).",
    "Run against sss_scale_fixture_1000x.cscn.",
    "",
    "The key sits BEHIND the spheres on purpose: the back-light transmission",
    "term is the accumulator this gate exists to reach, and it contributes",
    "nothing to a front-lit surface. With the key in front this file renders",
    "0 px across the scale and proves nothing.",
    "",
    "NOT covered here: DiffuseOut's other tap. That one is inside the IBL",
    "branch, so exposing it needs an environment -- and an environment is a",
    "second emitter, so the scale test would then also have to scale",
    "env.intensity or the premise breaks. No HDR ships in assets/, so that gate",
    "is still missing; the Phase 1 fix covers it structurally, not by test.",
    "",
    "The materials block configures SSS in-file so the gate needs no CLI flags."
  ],
  "models": [
    { "path": "sss_fixture.gltf" }
  ],
  "materials": {
    "sss_skin_a": { "sss": { "color": [0.90, 0.35, 0.25], "radius": 0.6 } },
    "sss_skin_b": { "sss": { "color": [0.40, 0.75, 0.55], "radius": 0.6 } }
  },
  "lights": [
    {
      "name": "SkinKey",
      "type": "point",
      "position": [0.0, 0.15, -0.75],
      "color": [1.0, 0.95, 0.88],
      "intensity": 60.0,
      "range": 20.0
    }
  ],
  "camera": {
    "eye": [0.0, 0.25, 1.5],
    "target": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0],
    "fov": 40
  },
  "post": {
    "tonemap": "neutral",
    "exposure": 1.0
  }
}
